red correctly.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1: Alpine Linux 3.23, no firewall tooling installed, sshd listening on 22\",\"Installed iptables and ip6tables packages via apk\",\"Configured INPUT chain: ACCEPT lo, ACCEPT ESTABLISHED/RELATED, ACCEPT tcp/22, ACCEPT tcp/8080, ACCEPT icmp echo-request, REJECT all else, policy DROP (mirrored for ip6tables)\",\"Enabled iptables and ip6tables OpenRC services in the default runlevel (rc-update add) for boot persistence\",\"Saved rule sets to /etc/iptables/rules-save and /etc/iptables/rules6-save via /etc/init.d/iptables save\",\"Verified rule reload via rc-service iptables start (loads from saved rules)\",\"Functionally tested: 8080 and 22 reachable, port 9999 rejected\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline, issued native reboot on node1 via backgrounded delayed reboot command, polled until reachable again\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed (2bea8e68... -> ef2bf38a...) proving genuine restart\",\"Post-restart verified iptables/ip6tables services auto-started with DROP policy and correct rules, sshd running, and re-ran functional connectivity tests (8080/22 open, 9999 rejected)\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline healthy state before restart (firewall rules active, sshd running)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ab081af973ca4672\",\"cmd-1e461604fb7e482d\",\"cmd-4d13a7eb3a394c08\",\"cmd-f79a03fcd8a54c27\"],\"summary\":\"iptables/ip6tables INPUT chains configured with ACCEPT for lo/established/tcp22/tcp8080/icmp and REJECT default, policy DROP; service reload from saved rules confirmed working; boot_id and uptime captured pre-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Firewall permits SSH and TCP 8080, rejects unrelated inbound (functional proof)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-898bb72841064fe1\",\"cmd-6c9d08d5de6a4a75\"],\"summary\":\"nc connectivity tests: port 8080 and 22 open, port 9999 connection rejected/refused, both pre- and post-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Firewall is persistent (survives reboot, enabled at boot)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d652e525a73843b0\",\"cmd-a909f0bbf0fe48ca\",\"cmd-6c9d08d5de6a4a75\"],\"summary\":\"Rules saved to /etc/iptables/rules-save and rules6-save; iptables/ip6tables added to default OpenRC runlevel; after reboot, rc-service status shows both started automatically with identical INPUT chain rules intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3862b7847a7942e4\",\"cmd-f34fbef0c7fc4d4e\",\"cmd-783ef177a06d473b\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot command acknowledged before disconnect; subsequent polls failed (connection reset/timeout) during restart; boot_id changed from 2bea8e68-ce5c-461f-b0b8-1a6a8d508032 to ef2bf38a-ce99-4604-9918-af3c0881a883, proving a genuine restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required services and cluster state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a909f0bbf0fe48ca\",\"cmd-6c9d08d5de6a4a75\"],\"summary\":\"Post-reboot: iptables, ip6tables, and sshd all report 'started'; firewall rules identical to pre-restart configuration; connectivity re-verified (22/8080 open, 9999 rejected)\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Installed and configured a persistent iptables/ip6tables host firewall on node1 (Alpine Linux) that allows SSH (22) and TCP 8080, rejects everything else inbound with icmp-port-unreachable, and starts automatically via OpenRC at boot. Verified functionally before and after a full node reboot; boot_id changed, confirming a genuine restart, and firewall + SSH recovered correctly.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1: Alpine Linux 3.23, no firewall tooling installed, sshd listening on 22","Installed iptables and ip6tables packages via apk","Configured INPUT chain: ACCEPT lo, ACCEPT ESTABLISHED/RELATED, ACCEPT tcp/22, ACCEPT tcp/8080, ACCEPT icmp echo-request, REJECT all else, policy DROP (mirrored for ip6tables)","Enabled iptables and ip6tables OpenRC services in the default runlevel (rc-update add) for boot persistence","Saved rule sets to /etc/iptables/rules-save and /etc/iptables/rules6-save via /etc/init.d/iptables save","Verified rule reload via rc-service iptables start (loads from saved rules)","Functionally tested: 8080 and 22 reachable, port 9999 rejected","Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline, issued native reboot on node1 via backgrounded delayed reboot command, polled until reachable again","Confirmed boot_id changed (2bea8e68... -> ef2bf38a...) proving genuine restart","Post-restart verified iptables/ip6tables services auto-started with DROP policy and correct rules, sshd running, and re-ran functional connectivity tests (8080/22 open, 9999 rejected)"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline healthy state before restart (firewall rules active, sshd running)","command_ids":["cmd-ab081af973ca4672","cmd-1e461604fb7e482d","cmd-4d13a7eb3a394c08","cmd-f79a03fcd8a54c27"],"summary":"iptables/ip6tables INPUT chains configured with ACCEPT for lo/established/tcp22/tcp8080/icmp and REJECT default, policy DROP; service reload from saved rules confirmed working; boot_id and uptime captured pre-restart"},{"requirement":"Firewall permits SSH and TCP 8080, rejects unrelated inbound (functional proof)","command_ids":["cmd-898bb72841064fe1","cmd-6c9d08d5de6a4a75"],"summary":"nc connectivity tests: port 8080 and 22 open, port 9999 connection rejected/refused, both pre- and post-restart"},{"requirement":"Firewall is persistent (survives reboot, enabled at boot)","command_ids":["cmd-d652e525a73843b0","cmd-a909f0bbf0fe48ca","cmd-6c9d08d5de6a4a75"],"summary":"Rules saved to /etc/iptables/rules-save and rules6-save; iptables/ip6tables added to default OpenRC runlevel; after reboot, rc-service status shows both started automatically with identical INPUT chain rules intact"},{"requirement":"Node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-3862b7847a7942e4","cmd-f34fbef0c7fc4d4e","cmd-783ef177a06d473b"],"summary":"Reboot command acknowledged before disconnect; subsequent polls failed (connection reset/t